# Doing Right Now

- Keep the journal primary: one timestamped line for the present moment that helps the user begin or resume.
- This is not a planner, to-do list, habit tracker, or project-management system.
- Judge features by whether they make it easier to write one line and do that.

## Product boundaries

- Projects and issues are optional plain-text support. `+Ongoing` is the permanent default workspace.
- Avoid statuses, assignees, due dates, boards, workflows, progress systems, and edit history unless explicitly requested.
- Prefer words users write themselves over structured metadata or required formats.
- Do not alter Today’s composer or current-entry row unless the request specifically requires it.

## Implementation

- The app is `DoingRightNow.html`: one dependency-free HTML file using IndexedDB and JSON import/export.
- Preserve existing journals and normalize old data without inventing historical timestamps.
- Keep visible timestamps purposeful; silent metadata must not complicate the UI.
- Do not modify `dev/` prototypes unless explicitly requested.
- Avoid new dependencies and build tooling.

## Completion

- Update in-app Help, `help.md`, and `help.html` when user-visible behavior changes.
- Keep landing-page copy aligned when the public feature set changes.
- Syntax-check the embedded script and verify affected existing flows.
